# contextpack project rules

## Using contextpack for codebase context

Before large refactors or when you need orientation on this codebase:

```bash
contextpack pack . --budget 8000 -o context.md
```

This generates a token-budgeted digest with prioritized file contents.

## Key directories

- `src/` — TypeScript source
- `tests/` — Vitest tests
- `docs/` — Documentation
- `fixtures/` — Demo fixtures

## Development

```bash
npm install
npm test
npm run build
```

Run tests before committing changes.
